 }

=== QB011 | assignment continued into a statement
f:{[]
 result:
 / continued assignment
 if[1b;1];
 result
 }

=== clean | expression conditional has a value
f:{[]
 result:
 $[1b;1;2];
 result
 }

=== QT001 | following unindented statement is not dictionary value
v:`a`b!1 2 3
1 2

=== clean | following unindented statement is not appended to dictionary value
v:`a`b!1 2
1 2 3

=== clean | an unindented block is a separate script expression
f:{[a;b]a+b}
[1;2;3]
til
[1.5]

=== clean | an indented line under a comment at the head of a file is comment (q 5: b stays undefined)
/ comment
  b:1+`a
c:2

=== clean | so are several, after a system command and more comment
\d .
/ one
/ two
  b:1+`a
  d:1+`a
c:2

=== clean | a blank line does not end that stretch (q 5 loads the file and b stays undefined)
/ comment

  b:1+`a

=== clean | nor does a system command, a whitespace-only line, or the start of the file (q 5: b undefined)
  a:1+`a
/ c

\d .foo
  b:1+`a
c:2

